            shf:hasEffectOn "protein synthesis, muscle repair, and regulating blood sugar" ;
            rdf:label "Leucine" ;
            rdfs:comment "Leucine is an essential amino acid, meaning the body cannot make it and must obtain it from food. It helps build and repair muscle, supports protein production, and plays a role in recovery after exercise or illness. Good sources include meat, fish, eggs, dairy products, soy, beans, nuts, and seeds." .


